{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_home_assistant", "label": "Home Assistant (docs/home-assistant.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "label": "Home Assistant integration (tools, prompt line, mute gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parlour's first integration, on by default under integrations['home-assistant'] with url, mcp, rest and muteEntity."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_mcp_server", "label": "HA Model Context Protocol Server (/mcp_server/sse)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## What Parlour can do with it", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Publishes whatever is exposed under Settings > Voice assistants > Expose as tools, so Parlour inherits it all with nothing to change on its side. If the MCP connection fails the REST tools remain, so the house is still reachable the slower way."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_rest_tools", "label": "REST escape hatches ha_get_state and ha_call_service", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## What Parlour can do with it", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For what intents cannot express; the prompt tells the model to prefer a more specific tool when one fits."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_ha_token", "label": "HA_TOKEN long-lived access token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "That token is the whole house, so it stays in secrets.env with mode 600 and never near git."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_openai_conversation", "label": "HA as a client via OpenAI Conversation (/v1, model parlour)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## Home Assistant as a client", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Home Assistant and every Voice PE satellite keep doing wake word, STT and speech back; only the thinking moves to Parlour. The prompt and temperature on the HA page are ignored because Parlour brings its own persona and tools. Each HA user gets a conversation of their own."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_mute_entity", "label": "muteEntity gate (fails open)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## Muting", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Parlour asks over REST after the wake word fires and before it acts, so the mute is enforced by the house rather than by the machine and covers every client alike. If the house cannot be reached the gate reads as off: a house that cannot be asked should still be able to hear you. A muted wake emits a muted event so the desktop app can explain why nothing happened."}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_rest_command_ask", "label": "HA rest_command ask_parlour to POST /ask", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## Home Assistant as a client", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_home_assistant_legacy_migration", "label": "Migration from agent.config.json", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## Moving over from the old configuration", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parlour init looks for agent.config.json in cwd and offers to convert: homeAssistant.* to integrations['home-assistant'], mcpServers to integrations.mcp.servers, search.searxngUrl to search.url, tts.engine say to macos-say, .env to secrets.env with AGENT_TOKEN renamed to PARLOUR_TOKEN. AGENT_TOKEN stays a fallback for one release so upgrading does not lock every phone and satellite out. The old default mute entity input_boolean.home_agent_muted is written out so the mute keeps working."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "docs_home_assistant_mcp_server", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## What Parlour can do with it", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "docs_home_assistant_rest_tools", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## What Parlour can do with it", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "docs_home_assistant_ha_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "docs_home_assistant_mute_entity", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "## Muting", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "docs_providers_integration_interface", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_home_assistant_integration", "target": "packages_parlour_src_integrations_home_assistant_index", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/home-assistant.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.